            <ArticleTitle>[Application of naropin (ropivacaine) for intra- and postoperative analgesia in phthysiosurgical patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>43-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The results of the analgesia method choice, as well as their combination, using a local anesthetic naropin (ropivacaine) for intra- and postoperative analgesia in phthysiosurgical patients, were analyzed. Application of the preparation have permitted to reduce the opioid analgetics dose by 50%, to realize the early mobilization in 50 - 70% patients, to reduce a postoperative morbidity rate, connected with the respiratory and digestive systems affection.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
